-- ----- fragment: minion_isaiah_43.sql (Isaiah 43) -----
-- Chapter: Isaiah 43 — THOU ART MINE / NO SAVIOUR BESIDE ME / A NEW THING. The chapter opens
-- *But now thus saith Yahuah (LORD) that created thee, O Jacob, and he that formed thee, O
-- Yashar'el (Israel), Fear not: for I have redeemed thee, I have called thee by thy name; thou
-- art mine* (43:1) — the Creator who FORMED Yashar'el redeems, names, and claims his people, and
-- carries them through water and fire unburned (43:2). At the heart stands the sole-Saviour
-- declaration: *I, even I, am Yahuah (LORD); and beside me there is no saviour* (43:11) — the
-- Formed and Formless lens: Yahuah is the ONLY Saviour, and that one salvation is wrought in the
-- Formed Son (Yahusha our Saviour, Titus 2:13), who is Yahuah and HAS a Father; never two
-- saviours, never a co-equal trinitarian second person, never modalism. The chapter gathers the
-- two houses from the four quarters (43:5-7) — Rom 11 guard, never replacement — announces the
-- NEW THING, a second exodus with rivers in the desert (43:18-19), and ends in pardon for His
-- own name's sake: *I, even I, am he that blotteth out thy transgressions for mine own sake, and
-- will not remember thy sins* (43:25) — pardon unto teshuvah, never licence (the Torah stands).
-- Tag: isa43   Temp view: _s303_isa43_lookup
-- Sort band: base 27050, step 3 -> threads at 27050, 27053, 27056, 27059, 27062 (5 threads)
-- Source of EVERY row: 'canon','isaiah',43,v
--
-- Isaiah 43 coverage:
--   ★ v.1-2 (created thee... formed thee... I have redeemed thee, I have called thee by thy name;
--          thou art mine... when thou walkest through the fire, thou shalt not be burned)
--        NT:     ★ 1 Peter 2:9 (a peculiar people... called you out of darkness) — THREAD 1
--                (the named, claimed people)
--        Extras: none warranted (clean canon weave; redemption-and-fire held in canon witnesses)
--        Tanakh: ★ Exodus 6:6 (I will redeem you with a stretched out arm) — THREAD 1 (the
--                redemption-name), ★ Psalm 66:12 (we went through fire and through water) +
--                Daniel 3:25,27 (the fire that did not burn — lateral) + Isaiah 44:21 lateral
--   ★★ v.10-12 (Ye are my witnesses... before me there was no Elohim (God) formed... I, even I,
--          am Yahuah (LORD); and beside me there is no saviour) — THE SOLE SAVIOUR
--        NT:     ★★ Acts 4:12 (neither is there salvation in any other), ★★ Titus 2:13-14 (our
--                Saviour Yahusha), ★★ 1 Timothy 2:5 (one Elohim, and one mediator), Acts 1:8 (ye
--                shall be witnesses unto me — lateral) — THREAD 2
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: ★ Hosea 13:4 (there is no saviour beside me) — THREAD 2
--   v.5-7 (I will bring thy seed from the east, and gather thee from the west... bring my sons
--          from far, and my daughters from the ends of the earth) — TWO-HOUSE INGATHERING
--        NT:     Matthew 8:11 (many shall come from the east and west), Mark 13:27 (gather his
--                elect from the four winds) — THREAD 3
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: ★ Isaiah 11:12 (assemble the outcasts of Yashar'el... the dispersed of Yahudah
--                from the four corners) — THREAD 3 (the two houses gathered, Rom 11 guard)
--   ★ v.18-19 (Remember ye not the former things... Behold, I will do a new thing... I will even
--          make a way in the wilderness, and rivers in the desert) — THE NEW THING / 2ND EXODUS
--        NT:     ★ 2 Corinthians 5:17 (a new creature... all things are become new), Revelation
--                21:5 (Behold, I make all things new) — THREAD 4
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: ★ Isaiah 48:21 (he caused the waters to flow out of the rock — waters in the
--                wilderness) — THREAD 4
--   ★★ v.25 (I, even I, am he that blotteth out thy transgressions for mine own sake, and will
--          not remember thy sins) — PARDON FOR HIS OWN NAME'S SAKE
--        NT:     ★ Acts 3:19 (that your sins may be blotted out) — THREAD 5
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: ★ Isaiah 44:22 (I have blotted out... thy transgressions), ★ Psalm 103:12 (as
--                far as the east is from the west), ★ Jeremiah 31:34 (I will remember their sin
--                no more) — THREAD 5 (pardon unto teshuvah, not licence)
--   v.3-4 (thy Saviour... thou hast been honourable, and I have loved thee) — woven into THREAD 1
--          and THREAD 2 prose (the Saviour-name + the love that redeems); no separate add.
--   v.8-9, v.13-17, v.20-24, v.26-28 (the witnesses summons, the way through the sea, the
--          weariness/sin indictment, the lawsuit) — held in prose, none silently skipped.
--
-- Threads (slug — target libraries):
--   1. isaiah-43-i-have-redeemed-thee-thou-art-mine — NT (1 Peter 2) + Tanakh (Exodus 6, Psalm
--      66, Daniel 3, Isaiah 44) [free] (★ created/formed/redeemed/named; fire that does not burn)
--   2. isaiah-43-beside-me-there-is-no-saviour — NT (Acts 4, Titus 2, 1 Timothy 2, Acts 1) +
--      Tanakh (Hosea 13) [free] (★★ the sole Saviour; Formed-and-Formless — one salvation in the
--      Formed Son who is Yahuah and has a Father)
--   3. isaiah-43-gather-thee-from-the-four-quarters — NT (Matthew 8, Mark 13) + Tanakh (Isaiah
--      11) [free] (the two-house ingathering from the four quarters; Rom 11 guard)
--   4. isaiah-43-behold-i-will-do-a-new-thing — NT (2 Corinthians 5, Revelation 21) + Tanakh
--      (Isaiah 48) [free] (★ the new thing; the second exodus, rivers in the desert)
--   5. isaiah-43-blotteth-out-thy-transgressions-for-mine-own-sake — NT (Acts 3) + Tanakh (Isaiah
--      44, Psalm 103, Jeremiah 31) [free] (★★ pardon for His own name's sake, unto teshuvah)
--
-- Framing notes:
--   ★ REDEEMED, NAMED, MINE (THREAD 1): *I have redeemed thee, I have called thee by thy name;
--      thou art mine* (43:1) — the redemption-name of Exodus 6:6 (*I will redeem you with a
--      stretched out arm*) made personal; the peculiar people of 1 Peter 2:9; the fire that did
--      not burn (Daniel 3) the historical proof of *when thou walkest through the fire, thou
--      shalt not be burned* (43:2).
--   ★★ THE SOLE SAVIOUR (THREAD 2): *beside me there is no saviour* (43:11) read with Hosea 13:4,
--      Acts 4:12, Titus 2:13-14, 1 Timothy 2:5. Framed STRICT: Yahuah is the ONLY Saviour, and
--      the one salvation is accomplished in the Formed Son — *our Saviour Yahusha HaMashiach*
--      (Titus 2:13) — who is Yahuah and has a Father; *one Elohim... one mediator... the man*
--      (1 Tim 2:5). Never two saviours; never co-equal persons; never modalism.
--   TWO-HOUSE INGATHERING (THREAD 3): *bring my sons from far, and my daughters from the ends of
--      the earth* (43:6) = Isaiah 11:12's outcasts of Yashar'el + dispersed of Yahudah, the two
--      houses, never a new replacement people (Rom 11:1-2).
--   ★ THE NEW THING (THREAD 4): *Behold, I will do a new thing... rivers in the desert* (43:19) —
--      the second exodus (Isaiah 48:21 waters from the rock); 2 Corinthians 5:17 / Revelation
--      21:5 the new creation it opens toward.
--   ★★ PARDON FOR HIS OWN NAME'S SAKE (THREAD 5): *for mine own sake, and will not remember thy
--      sins* (43:25) = Isaiah 44:22 / Jeremiah 31:34 / Psalm 103:12; Acts 3:19's blotting-out is
--      *Repent ye therefore, and be converted* — pardon unto teshuvah, never licence; the Torah
--      written on the heart stands (Jer 31:33), the new covenant the same Torah, not Torah replaced.

CREATE TEMP VIEW _s303_isa43_lookup AS
SELECT e.slug AS edition_slug, b.slug AS book_slug, c.chapter_number, v.verse_number, v.id AS verse_id
  FROM verses v JOIN chapters c ON v.chapter_id=c.id JOIN books b ON c.book_id=b.id
  JOIN editions e ON b.edition_id=e.id
 WHERE e.slug IN ('canon','enoch','jubilees','jasher','apocrypha','apocrypha-charles-vol1','pseudepigrapha','adam-eve-conflict','apocalypse-of-abraham','ascension-isaiah','sonnini-acts-29');

INSERT INTO cross_references (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source, note, tier_required)
SELECT sv.verse_id, tv.verse_id, 'manual', i.note, i.tier::content_tier
  FROM (VALUES
    -- THREAD 1 (★): I have redeemed thee, thou art mine (created/formed/named; the fire unburned)
    ('canon','isaiah',43,1,'canon','exodus',6,6,'free',
      E'*Wherefore say unto the children of Yashar''el (Israel), I am Yahuah (LORD), and I will bring you out from under the burdens of the Egyptians, and I will rid you out of their bondage, and I will redeem you with a stretched out arm, and with great judgments* (Exodus 6:6). The redemption Isaiah makes personal — *I have redeemed thee, I have called thee by thy name; thou art mine* (Isaiah 43:1) — is the very covenant-word Yahuah swore at the exodus: *I will redeem you with a stretched out arm*. The Creator who *formed thee, O Yashar''el (Israel)* is the same Redeemer who brought them out and called them his own.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',43,1,'canon','1-peter',2,9,'free',
      E'*But ye are a chosen generation, a royal priesthood, an holy nation, a peculiar people; that ye should shew forth the praises of him who hath called you out of darkness into his marvellous light* (1 Peter 2:9). The people *called by thy name; thou art mine* (Isaiah 43:1) are the *peculiar people* Peter names — claimed, chosen, called out by the One who *formed thee*. To be redeemed and named by Yahuah is to be *an holy nation*, his own possession to shew forth his praise.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',43,2,'canon','psalms',66,12,'free',
      E'*Thou hast caused men to ride over our heads; we went through fire and through water: but thou broughtest us out into a wealthy place* (Psalm 66:12). The promise *When thou passest through the waters, I will be with thee... when thou walkest through the fire, thou shalt not be burned* (Isaiah 43:2) is the testimony Israel already sings: *we went through fire and through water: but thou broughtest us out*. The waters do not overflow and the fire does not consume because Yahuah is with his redeemed in the midst of them.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',43,2,'canon','daniel',3,25,'free',
      E'*He answered and said, Lo, I see four men loose, walking in the midst of the fire, and they have no hurt; and the form of the fourth is like the Son of Elohim (God)* (Daniel 3:25). The word *when thou walkest through the fire, thou shalt not be burned* (Isaiah 43:2) is shown in the furnace of Babylon: three men walk *in the midst of the fire... no hurt*, and a fourth is with them — *the form of the fourth is like the Son of Elohim (God)*, the Formed Son who stands with his own in the flame. *I will be with thee* is not a figure; it is the Presence in the fire.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',43,2,'canon','daniel',3,27,'free',
      E'*And the princes, governors, and captains, and the king''s counsellors, being gathered together, saw these men, upon whose bodies the fire had no power, nor was an hair of their head singed, neither were their coats changed, nor the smell of fire had passed on them* (Daniel 3:27). Isaiah''s *neither shall the flame kindle upon thee* (Isaiah 43:2) is fulfilled to the letter — *the fire had no power... nor was an hair of their head singed... nor the smell of fire had passed on them*. The redeemed pass through the flame and it does not so much as scorch them, for Yahuah is with them.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',43,1,'canon','isaiah',44,21,'free',
      E'*Remember these, O Jacob and Yashar''el (Israel); for thou art my servant: I have formed thee; thou art my servant: O Yashar''el (Israel), thou shalt not be forgotten of me* (Isaiah 44:21). The chapter''s own next word doubles the claim of *he that formed thee, O Yashar''el (Israel)... thou art mine* (Isaiah 43:1): *I have formed thee; thou art my servant... thou shalt not be forgotten of me*. The Creator who formed his people will not forget them — the one He formed, He keeps as His own.'),

    -- THREAD 2 (★★): Beside me there is no saviour (the sole Saviour; Formed and Formless)
    ('canon','isaiah',43,11,'canon','hosea',13,4,'free',
      E'*Yet I am Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) from the land of Egypt, and thou shalt know no god but me: for there is no saviour beside me* (Hosea 13:4). Hosea speaks the very declaration of *I, even I, am Yahuah (LORD); and beside me there is no saviour* (Isaiah 43:11). One word, two prophets: Yahuah alone saves — *there is no saviour beside me* — and to look for salvation in any other is to forget the God who brought Israel up from Egypt.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',43,11,'canon','acts',4,12,'free',
      E'*Neither is there salvation in any other: for there is none other name under heaven given among men, whereby we must be saved* (Acts 4:12). Peter''s declaration is Isaiah''s own — *beside me there is no saviour* (Isaiah 43:11) — now spoken of the name in which Yahuah''s salvation is wrought: *none other name under heaven... whereby we must be saved*. This is not a second saviour but the ONE salvation of the ONE Saviour, accomplished in the Formed Son who bears the Name.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',43,11,'canon','titus',2,13,'free',
      E'*Looking for that blessed hope, and the glorious appearing of the great Elohim (God) and our Saviour Yahusha HaMashiach (Jesus Christ)* (Titus 2:13). When Yahuah says *beside me there is no saviour* (Isaiah 43:11), and the apostle names *our Saviour Yahusha HaMashiach (Jesus Christ)*, there is no contradiction: the Formed Son IS Yahuah the only Saviour, the visible appearing of the One who said *I, even I, am Yahuah (LORD)*. The Saviour who appears is Yahuah; he is Yahuah and has a Father — not a second saviour, not a co-equal person.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',43,11,'canon','titus',2,14,'free',
      E'*Who gave himself for us, that he might redeem us from all iniquity, and purify unto himself a peculiar people, zealous of good works* (Titus 2:14). The sole Saviour of *beside me there is no saviour* (Isaiah 43:11) is the One who *gave himself for us, that he might redeem us* — the redemption of 43:1 carried to its end. And it purifies *a peculiar people, zealous of good works*: pardon unto obedience, never licence; the redeemed are made zealous for the very commandments, the Torah written on the heart.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',43,10,'canon','1-timothy',2,5,'free',
      E'*For there is one Elohim (God), and one mediator between Elohim (God) and men, the man HaMashiach Yahusha (Christ Jesus)* (1 Timothy 2:5). Isaiah''s *before me there was no Elohim (God) formed, neither shall there be after me* (Isaiah 43:10) guards the oneness Paul confesses: *one Elohim (God), and one mediator... the man*. The Formed Son is that one mediator — the man who is Yahuah and has a Father; not a second deity *formed* alongside the Most High, but the expressed Word who stands between, who is Himself Yahuah.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',43,10,'canon','acts',1,8,'free',
      E'*But ye shall receive power, after that the Ruach HaKodesh (Holy Spirit) is come upon you: and ye shall be witnesses unto me both in Jerusalem, and in all Judæa, and in Samaria, and unto the uttermost part of the earth* (Acts 1:8). Yahuah calls his people *Ye are my witnesses, saith Yahuah (LORD), and my servant whom I have chosen* (Isaiah 43:10); the risen Son sends the same commission — *ye shall be witnesses unto me*. The witnesses who testify *that I am he* now bear witness to the uttermost part of the earth that Yahuah alone is the Saviour, made known in the Formed Son.'),

    -- THREAD 3: Gather thee from the four quarters (the two-house ingathering)
    ('canon','isaiah',43,6,'canon','isaiah',11,12,'free',
      E'*And he shall set up an ensign for the nations, and shall assemble the outcasts of Yashar''el (Israel), and gather together the dispersed of Yahudah (Judah) from the four corners of the earth* (Isaiah 11:12). The four-quarters ingathering of *I will bring thy seed from the east, and gather thee from the west; I will say to the north, Give up; and to the south, Keep not back* (Isaiah 43:5-6) is the two-house regathering: *the outcasts of Yashar''el (Israel)* (the scattered northern house) and *the dispersed of Yahudah (Judah)* assembled *from the four corners*. The sons from far and daughters from the ends of the earth are the divided houses brought home as one.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',43,5,'canon','matthew',8,11,'free',
      E'*And I say unto you, That many shall come from the east and west, and shall sit down with Abraham, and Isaac, and Jacob, in the kingdom of heaven* (Matthew 8:11). Yahusha echoes the ingathering of *I will bring thy seed from the east, and gather thee from the west* (Isaiah 43:5): *many shall come from the east and west, and shall sit down with Abraham, and Isaac, and Jacob*. The scattered seed of the patriarchs is gathered from the quarters to the table of the fathers — the regathering of the covenant people, never their replacement.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',43,6,'canon','mark',13,27,'free',
      E'*And then shall he send his angels, and shall gather together his elect from the four winds, from the uttermost part of the earth to the uttermost part of heaven* (Mark 13:27). The word *bring my sons from far, and my daughters from the ends of the earth* (Isaiah 43:6) is consummated when the Son of Adam *shall gather together his elect from the four winds, from the uttermost part of the earth*. The four quarters of Isaiah become the four winds of the ingathering — the chosen people, *every one that is called by my name* (43:7), assembled home.'),

    -- THREAD 4 (★): Behold, I will do a new thing (the new thing; the second exodus)
    ('canon','isaiah',43,19,'canon','2-corinthians',5,17,'free',
      E'*Therefore if any man be in Messiah (Christ), he is a new creature: old things are passed away; behold, all things are become new* (2 Corinthians 5:17). The promise *Remember ye not the former things... Behold, I will do a new thing* (Isaiah 43:18-19) opens toward this: in the Messiah *old things are passed away; behold, all things are become new*. The new thing that springs forth in the wilderness is the renewing work of the Redeemer — a new creation rising where the former things are not remembered.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',43,19,'canon','revelation',21,5,'free',
      E'*And he that sat upon the throne said, Behold, I make all things new. And he said unto me, Write: for these words are true and faithful* (Revelation 21:5). Isaiah''s *Behold, I will do a new thing; now it shall spring forth* (Isaiah 43:19) reaches its end in the throne-word *Behold, I make all things new*. The new thing that begins as *a way in the wilderness, and rivers in the desert* is consummated in the new heaven and new earth, where the former things are passed away forever.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',43,19,'canon','isaiah',48,21,'free',
      E'*And they thirsted not when he led them through the deserts: he caused the waters to flow out of the rock for them: he clave the rock also, and the waters gushed out* (Isaiah 48:21). The new thing of *rivers in the desert* (Isaiah 43:19) is the second-exodus pattern Isaiah names again: *he caused the waters to flow out of the rock for them... and the waters gushed out*. As in the first exodus, so in the new — Yahuah makes a way and gives water in the wilderness to his redeemed, *to give drink to my people, my chosen* (43:20).'),

    -- THREAD 5 (★★): Blotteth out thy transgressions for mine own sake (pardon for His name's sake)
    ('canon','isaiah',43,25,'canon','isaiah',44,22,'free',
      E'*I have blotted out, as a thick cloud, thy transgressions, and, as a cloud, thy sins: return unto me; for I have redeemed thee* (Isaiah 44:22). The pardon of *I, even I, am he that blotteth out thy transgressions for mine own sake* (Isaiah 43:25) is sealed in the next chapter: *I have blotted out, as a thick cloud, thy transgressions... return unto me*. The blotting-out is unto teshuvah — *return unto me; for I have redeemed thee* — pardon that calls the redeemed home, never licence to sin.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',43,25,'canon','acts',3,19,'free',
      E'*Repent ye therefore, and be converted, that your sins may be blotted out, when the times of refreshing shall come from the presence of Yahuah (Lord)* (Acts 3:19). Peter preaches Isaiah''s pardon — *that your sins may be blotted out* — exactly as *I... am he that blotteth out thy transgressions* (Isaiah 43:25), and exactly unto turning: *Repent ye therefore, and be converted*. The blotting-out of sins is bound to teshuvah; the pardon for His own name''s sake is received in returning, not in remaining in sin.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',43,25,'canon','psalms',103,12,'free',
      E'*As far as the east is from the west, so far hath he removed our transgressions from us* (Psalm 103:12). To *blot out thy transgressions... and will not remember thy sins* (Isaiah 43:25) is the mercy the psalm measures: *As far as the east is from the west, so far hath he removed our transgressions from us*. The sins Yahuah will not remember are carried away beyond return — a pardon as wide as the heavens, *for mine own sake*.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',43,25,'canon','jeremiah',31,34,'free',
      E'*And they shall teach no more every man his neighbour, and every man his brother, saying, Know Yahuah (LORD): for they shall all know me, from the least of them unto the greatest of them, saith Yahuah (LORD): for I will forgive their iniquity, and I will remember their sin no more* (Jeremiah 31:34). Isaiah''s *will not remember thy sins* (Isaiah 43:25) is the new-covenant promise: *I will forgive their iniquity, and I will remember their sin no more*. And the same covenant writes the Torah on the heart — *I will put my law in their inward parts* (31:33): the sin is remembered no more, and the law is kept from within. Pardon and obedience together, not pardon instead of obedience.')
  ) AS i(src_edition,src_slug,src_ch,src_v,tgt_edition,tgt_slug,tgt_ch,tgt_v,tier,note)
  JOIN _s303_isa43_lookup sv ON sv.edition_slug=i.src_edition AND sv.book_slug=i.src_slug AND sv.chapter_number=i.src_ch AND sv.verse_number=i.src_v
  JOIN _s303_isa43_lookup tv ON tv.edition_slug=i.tgt_edition AND tv.book_slug=i.tgt_slug AND tv.chapter_number=i.tgt_ch AND tv.verse_number=i.tgt_v
 WHERE sv.verse_id <> tv.verse_id
ON CONFLICT (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 1 (★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-43-i-have-redeemed-thee-thou-art-mine',
       E'I have redeemed thee, thou art mine — the formed people named through fire and water',
       E'The chapter opens with the Creator claiming his own: *But now thus saith Yahuah (LORD) that created thee, O Jacob, and he that formed thee, O Yashar''el (Israel), Fear not: for I have redeemed thee, I have called thee by thy name; thou art mine* (Isaiah 43:1). The redemption is the covenant-word sworn at the exodus: *I will redeem you with a stretched out arm, and with great judgments* (Exodus 6:6). The named, claimed people are the *peculiar people* who *shew forth the praises of him who hath called you out of darkness* (1 Peter 2:9). And the promise that follows is no figure: *When thou passest through the waters, I will be with thee; and through the rivers, they shall not overflow thee: when thou walkest through the fire, thou shalt not be burned; neither shall the flame kindle upon thee* (43:2). Israel already sings it — *we went through fire and through water: but thou broughtest us out into a wealthy place* (Psalm 66:12) — and the furnace of Babylon shows it to the letter: *Lo, I see four men loose, walking in the midst of the fire, and they have no hurt; and the form of the fourth is like the Son of Elohim (God)* (Daniel 3:25); *the fire had no power... nor was an hair of their head singed... nor the smell of fire had passed on them* (Daniel 3:27). The Formed Son stands with his redeemed in the flame. And the chapter''s own next word keeps the claim: *I have formed thee; thou art my servant... thou shalt not be forgotten of me* (Isaiah 44:21).',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 27050
  FROM _s303_isa43_lookup sv, _s303_isa43_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=43 AND sv.verse_number=1
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=43 AND ev.verse_number=2
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 2 (★★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-43-beside-me-there-is-no-saviour',
       E'Beside me there is no saviour — Yahuah alone saves, in the Formed Son',
       E'At the heart of the chapter stands the sole-Saviour declaration: *Ye are my witnesses, saith Yahuah (LORD), and my servant whom I have chosen: that ye may know and believe me, and understand that I am he: before me there was no Elohim (God) formed, neither shall there be after me. I, even I, am Yahuah (LORD); and beside me there is no saviour* (Isaiah 43:10-11). Hosea speaks the same word: *there is no saviour beside me* (Hosea 13:4). This is the lens for everything the apostles confess. When Peter declares *Neither is there salvation in any other: for there is none other name under heaven given among men, whereby we must be saved* (Acts 4:12), and when Paul names *our Saviour Yahusha HaMashiach (Jesus Christ)* (Titus 2:13), there is no second saviour beside Yahuah — there is the ONE Saviour, Yahuah, whose one salvation is accomplished in the Formed Son. The Formed Son IS Yahuah the only Saviour, the visible appearing of the One who said *I, even I, am Yahuah (LORD)*; he is Yahuah and has a Father — *one Elohim (God), and one mediator between Elohim (God) and men, the man HaMashiach Yahusha (Christ Jesus)* (1 Timothy 2:5). Not a second deity *formed* alongside the Most High (43:10 forbids it), not co-equal persons, not modalism. And he *gave himself for us, that he might redeem us from all iniquity, and purify unto himself a peculiar people, zealous of good works* (Titus 2:14). The witnesses Yahuah chose to testify *that I am he* are sent by the risen Son to bear the same witness: *ye shall be witnesses unto me... unto the uttermost part of the earth* (Acts 1:8).',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 27053
  FROM _s303_isa43_lookup sv, _s303_isa43_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=43 AND sv.verse_number=10
